<article class="env-lemma" id="05NJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05NJ">Lemma <span data-tag="05NJ">17.17.8</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{F}'' \to \mathcal{F}' \to \mathcal{F} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> be a short exact sequence of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Assume $\mathcal{F}$ is flat. Then for any $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{G}$ the sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{F}'' \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}' \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{G} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using that $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module for every $x \in X$ and that exactness can be checked on stalks, this follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HL" data-tag="00HL">10.39.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>